Here's another usefull tool to use with the most Professional and Complete
Bulletin Board System Software for the Amiga, Excelsior!

I guess I dont have to explain to you what 'The Wall' does. So I'll just skip
to the installation proccess.

You can run 'The Wall' at each user's login or logout or whatever you wish.
All you have to do is Edit you language files. For example:

Original ENGLISH Language file has this at line 105:

\n1\q1Login complete\n1

Edit this line so that is stays like this:

\#2C:TheWall\n1\q1Login complete\n1

You'll have to copy 'TheWall' into your C: directory in this case.
You can also make 'The Wall' an user command. It's all up to your imagination.
What you HAVE to do is copy the files in the 's' directory to your s:
directory. These files are:

TheWall.header - Header to be displayed.
TheWall.data - Where the Wall data is.
TheWall.footer - End of display here.

Ok, I think everything's ready to run. I have to excuse for this lousy
documentation but I really dont think you need anything better, do ya? :-)

This product is 100% Public Domain. Spread it as you like as long as you
dont ask money for it. The source code is included in this version but
